    "chunk_text": "Sir, I would say that we cannot resolve the issues in our country and take the country forward unless we move away from debt and bring in FDIs into the country. Hon. Minister, your Ministry is the backbone of the economy. We have to bring in FDIs and to develop industries. Our closest neighbour, India, has the largest population in the world. We have a Free Trade Agreement with India. We must start industrial zones and give investors incentives. Unfortunately, every successive government felt that investors are waiting to come and start industries in Sri Lanka. But, our energy and labour costs are so high that we need to create a mechanism through which we give incentives to investors for industries to be set up in Sri Lanka.\n\nAlso, Hon. Minister, a lot of investors have come to Sri Lanka because there is a dispute recognition mechanism of arbitration. But, there are issues with regard to arbitration. If you take the Arbitration Act, there is no provision to get interim relief and certain arbitrations take a long duration of time. Also, arbitration has become a very costly process. So, I think there needs to be a centre set up by the State by which the cost of\n\n3125 3126\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0da7\u0dca\u0db1\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0dc1\u0dc3\u0d9b\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dda \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd4 19"
