    "chunk_index": 103,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "0b726d8636e5c5f04a8f3183ffcdd7ad",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1832,
    "chunk_text": "When we stood accused relating to the final phase of the war in Puthumathalan and Mullivaikkal, the entire international community was urged by western countries and many others, even our diaspora, to take action against us. Now, we also have to conscientiously stand up against\n\n3455 3456\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dae\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nSir, these most abominable and most horrendous at-tacks on Gaza and the hapless Palestinians should stop immediately. It is important that Sri Lanka should join growing international call for an immediate ceasefire, to stop hostilities and to prioritize humanitarian aid. Sir, our country should also support the demand for accountability for violations of international humanitarian and human rights law by the Israelies. We are a nation that has given moral leadership to the cause of Palestine over decades. We should now cast off the recent months\u2019 strategic stu-por, make our presence felt in the anti-colonial, anti-occupation camp of independent nations and demonstrate leadership to the international community, especially smaller nations, to amplify their voices and push for jus-tice and peace. There are increasing calls globally for arms embargoes and sanctions against Israel. Sri Lanka needs to watch developments carefully and should study what it could do to help achieve peace in the wider region through restoring our one-time globally acclaimed dis-armament and non-proliferation leadership.\n\nSo, as a responsible nation, it is prudent without fur-ther delay to do all that is possible to keep Palestine and its people from falling victim to Israeli strategic designs. We cannot be so gullible as to be made enemy of each other and to cause mayhem and chaos in this country just because there is love for Israeli money and their invest-ments in our land and on infrastructure."
