    "chunk_text": "\u0dc0\u0dd8\u0dca \u0dad\u0dd3 8 \u0d9c\u0dab\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db0\u0dd2\u0dae\u0dcf\u0dd2\u0db48 \u0dba \u0db1\u0dcf8 \u0db3\u0dcf8 \u0d85\u0db8\u0dcf\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dca 8\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dc1\u0dba \u0dc3\u0dca\u0dc0\u0dae\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0db8\u0d9c\u0dca\u0db0\u0db18 \u0db3\u0dcf\u0db8 \u0ddd\u0d9c\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0db8\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca8 \u0dc3\u0dd4\u0dc5\u0dd48 \u0dcf\u0dcf8 \u0db1\u0db0\u0dba8\u0db4\u0dd2\u0db4\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dab8 \u0dc0\u0dba\u0dc0\u0db3\u0dcf \u0dae \u0db1\u0dca\u0db8\u0d9c\u0dca\u0db0\u0db18 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dba8 \u0dbb\u0db8\u0dda\u0dc1\u0dba \u0dc38 \u0dcf\u0dd0\u0d9a\u0dd2 \u0dcf\u0dc08\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dca\u0db0\u0dcf 8 \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dd3\u0d9a\u0db1\u0da78 \u0db3\u0dcf\u0dcf 8 \u0dc0\u0dd3\u0db18 \u0db3\u0dc4\u0dcf\u0dcf8 \u0d85\u0dc0\u0dc1\u0dba \u0dc3\u0dba8 \u0dc0\u0dd0\u0da98\u0db4\u0dd2\u0dc5\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dc0\u0dc5\u0d9a\u0dca8 \u0db8\u0dbd\u0db38 \u0d94\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dca\u0db8\u0d9c\u0dca\u0db0\u0db18 capacity \u0da7\u0dae8 \u0d85\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dc08\u0db8\u200d\u0dbb\u0dda\u0dab\u0dd2\u0d9c\u0db18 \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dd3\u0d9a\u0db8\u0dda8 \u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dab \u0d9a\u0dca8 -8 score card system \u0da7\u0dae\u0d9a\u0dca8-8introduce \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dd3\u0d9a\u0db1\u0da78\u0dca\u200d\u0dd0\u0dcf\u0da7\u0db1\u0dca 8\u0dae\u0da7\u0dba\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dd48\u0dd6 \u0dca\u200d\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dda8\u0dae\u0db8\u0dbd\u0dcf8\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0db8\u0db6\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dcf.\n\n\u0db8\u0dda8 \u0dbb\u0dc1\u0dba \u0dc3\u0dca\u0dcf\u0db8 8 \u0db1\u0dc08 \u0db8\u0dae\u0ddc\u0da7\u0db3\u0d9a\u0dca8 \u0dd2\u0d9a\u0db6\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf 8 \u0dca\u200d\u0dd0\u0dcf\u0da78 \u0dd2\u0d9a\u0db8\u0db6\u0dcf8reciprocal tariff \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0da7\u0dbd\u0dd4\u0dc08 \u0db3\u0dda\u0db6\u0db1\u0dca\u0db0\u0dc08 \u0d85\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dcf.8 \u0da7\u0dae\u0da78 \u0db3\u0dca\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0db88\u0db1\u0dd2\u0db8 \u0ddd\u0d9c80((0)8 \u0da7\u0db8\u0dca 8\u0db8\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0db1\u0db18\u0dbb\u0dc1\u0dba \u0dc3\u0dca\u0dcf \u0d9a\u0dca8\u0db8 \u0ddc\u0db8\u0dd48\u0db8\u0dc0\u0dbd\u0dcf8\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0db8\u0db6\u0dcf8\u0db1\u0dd2\u0db3\u0dcf8 \u0db1\u0db18 \u0dc4\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dcf 8 \u0da7\u0da78 \u0d85\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf\u0dc58 \u0dc0\u0dd0 \u0daf\u0dd4\u0db88 \u0dd2\u0dbd\u0db3\u0dca\u0db1\u0db88 \u0db3\u0dda\u0db6\u0db1\u0dca\u0db0\u0db8 \u0db1\u0dca8\u0db3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0dc08\u0dca\u200d\u0dd0\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dc0\u0dca 8\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dd3\u0d9a\u0db1\u0da78\u0da7\u0db1\u0dd0\u0dcf\u0daf\u0dd38\u0dae\u0da7\u0dba\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dd48\u0db8\u0dae8\u0db8\u0db8\u0dd4\u0dc08\u0d87\u0db18\u0d9a\u0dd2 \u0dbd\u0dcf.\n\n\u0db8\u0db6\u0ddc\u0db8\u0dcf\u0ddc\u0db18\u0db3\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dba\u0dd2. \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dcf8\u0db1\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dca\u200d\u0dba8\u0dae\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0d85\u0dcf\u0dba\u0dae\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dcf\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0bc6\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) The second Question under Standing Order No. 27(2), the Hon. Ravi Karunanayake.\n\nII\n\n\u0d91\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dca8\u0da2\u0dca\u200d\u0d85\u0db4 8\u0d85\u0db8\u0d85\u0dba\u0ddd\u0d85\u0dba8\u0dbb\u0dab\u0dc0\u0dcf8\u0db6\u0daf\u0dd48\u0db4\u0dd0\u0d85\u0dc0\u0dd3\u0dcf8\n\n\u0dc3\u0dda\u0db6\u0db1\u0dca\u0db0\u0db8\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca8\u0dbb\u0dcf8\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dad\u0dd48\u0d8b\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dba\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbb8 \u0b90\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbf\u0baf \u0b85\u0b9a\u0bae\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95 \u0baa\u0bb0\u0bb8\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb0 \u0ba4\u0bc0\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0bae\u0bb5 \u0bb5\u0bbe\u0bbf \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bae\u0bae\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbe\u0b95 \u0b8e\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f \u0b9a\u0bb5\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bbf\u0baf\n\n\u0b89\u0baa\u0bbe\u0baf\u0bae\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bb1\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd COUNTER-STRATEGIES TO BE ADOPTED ON US RECIPORAL\n\nTARIFFS\n\n\u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dcf8\u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd38\u0dae\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dda\u0dcf\u0d85\u0dcf\u0dba\u0dae8\u0dcf\u0dd4\u0dcf\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Hon. Deputy Speaker, thank you very much for giving me this opportunity. I would like to ask this Question on the impact of the 44 per cent tax on Sri Lankan exports to the United States from the Hon. Minister of Finance.\n\n65 66\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s export sector, particularly that of the textile and apparel industry, has long relied on access to the US market as a key driver of economic growth. Given our fragile economic situation and our ongoing recovery from bankruptcy, maintaining stable trade relations with key partners is crucial and is a must for sustaining employment, foreign exchange inflows and overall economic stability."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2025-04-08-2025-04-08",
    "num": "2025-04-08",
    "date_str": "2025-04-08",
    "description": "Hansard of April 08, 2025",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1747715041076408.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-04-08-2025-04-08-0171",
    "chunk_index": 171,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "2fb00f939b0eecd2abc2af96e338d26c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1902,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s export sector, particularly that of the textile and apparel industry, has long relied on access to the US market as a key driver of economic growth. Given our fragile economic situation and our ongoing recovery from bankruptcy, maintaining stable trade relations with key partners is crucial and is a must for sustaining employment, foreign exchange inflows and overall economic stability.\n\nIt is imperative that the Government provides clarity on its preparedness, response and future course of action in addressing this critical issue. In that regard, could the Hon. Minister inform this House,\n\n1. Proactive Measures: After I raised this Question on the 18th of March, 2025, what immediate diplomatic or trade- related actions were taken by the Government to prevent such a drastic tariff imposition?\n\n2. Counter-strategies: In response to the newly imposed 44 per cent tax, what short-term and long-term counter-strategies will the Government adopt to protect Sri Lanka\u2019s export sector, rubber-based items, tea, marine exports (export of fish et cetera) and particularly the textile and apparel industries?\n\n3. Engagement with US Officials: Since my Question was raised, with whom in the US administration, the US Trade Representative (USTR) or other relevant authorities, has the Government engaged in discussions regarding this tariff hike and what has been the outcome of those engagements?\n\n4. Diplomatic Engagements and Negotiations with the US: Given that Sri Lanka is still emerging from bankruptcy, has the Government formally requested President Trump or the US administration to consider a special dispensation or an exemption for Sri Lankan exports?\n\n5. Market Diversification: Given the volatility of the US trade policy, what are the alternative export markets or trade agreements the Government is actively pursuing to reduce Sri Lanka\u2019s dependence on the US market?"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2025-04-08-2025-04-08",
    "num": "2025-04-08",
    "date_str": "2025-04-08",
    "description": "Hansard of April 08, 2025",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1747715041076408.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-04-08-2025-04-08-0172",
    "chunk_index": 172,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "b96caecb27cc6dc60195a71068a368f0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1716,
    "chunk_text": "5. Market Diversification: Given the volatility of the US trade policy, what are the alternative export markets or trade agreements the Government is actively pursuing to reduce Sri Lanka\u2019s dependence on the US market?\n\n6. Detailed Export Data: Over the past five years, what have been the primary products exported from Sri Lanka to the United States and what has been the export value for each of those products on an annual basis?\n\n7. Tariff Comparisons: What are the current tariff rates imposed by the United States on imports from Sri Lanka\u2019s main competitors in the textile and apparel sector and specifically on countries such as Indonesia, China, African countries, Vietnam, Bangladesh and India? How do these rates compare with the 44 per cent tariff now imposed on Sri Lankan exports? 8. Strategic Response: Given the competitive disadvantage posed by the higher tariffs on Sri Lankan exports, what are the specific strategies the Government is implementing to enhance the competitiveness of our export sector in the US market? As asked before, I am referring to the interest rates et cetera which have been mentioned here. 9. Support for Exporters: What measures are being taken to support Sri Lankan exporters affected by these tariffs, particularly the small and medium-sized enterprises which may be disproportionately impacted?\n\nSir, I know this is a national problem. I heard the Leader of the Opposition requesting that we convene an All-Party Conference on this matter. So, let us take this as a national crisis. You would not be able to take the world on. So, let the world pay attention to those particular areas where they are trying to impose taxes in a very capricious manner.\n\nThank you."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2025-04-08-2025-04-08",
    "num": "2025-04-08",
    "date_str": "2025-04-08",
    "description": "Hansard of April 08, 2025",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1747715041076408.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-04-08-2025-04-08-0173",
    "chunk_index": 173,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "f18d1e55b398ccd10b216518f86affd7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2027,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, I know this is a national problem. I heard the Leader of the Opposition requesting that we convene an All-Party Conference on this matter. So, let us take this as a national crisis. You would not be able to take the world on. So, let the world pay attention to those particular areas where they are trying to impose taxes in a very capricious manner.\n\nThank you.\n\nDiplomatic relations and continuous dialogues with the White House and the Office of the US Trade Representative have been taking place continuously. To highlight some of the actions we have taken, diplomatic measures have been taken on 14th February, 2025. The Sri Lankan Ambassador to the United States has engaged with continuous discussions and based on the outcome of those discussions, a particular report had been sent to us, which we have evaluated. Then, there has been another engagement with the International Monetary Fund as well just to highlight the significance of this issue since we are working under an EFF Programme of the IMF. There was another meeting held on Trade Policy Analysis and Strategic Alternatives on 28th March, 2025. At that meeting, the Embassy undertook a comprehensive review of Sri Lanka\u2019s current import profile from the United States and analysed US export performances globally. It was observed that most of the US goods are already subject to relative para-tariffs, but not other tariffs. Accordingly, some proposals have also been made. Then, on 01st April, 2025, the Sri Lankan Embassy engaged with the Office of the US Trade Representative, in which discussions Mr. Brendan Lynch, Assistant United States Trade Representative for South and Central Asia and Ms.\n\n67 68\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd48\u0db8\u0dc0\u0dd38\u0dae\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dcf \u0dae8\u0db1\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0d85\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dda\u0dbd\u0dca 08\n\nEmily Ashby, Director for South and Central Asia took part. Immediately responding to the Executive Order of 02nd April, 2025 or once this announcement was made, the particular Report was submitted. So, that is with regard to the diplomatic relations."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2025-04-08-2025-04-08",
    "num": "2025-04-08",
    "date_str": "2025-04-08",
    "description": "Hansard of April 08, 2025",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1747715041076408.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-04-08-2025-04-08-0174",
    "chunk_index": 174,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "d7dbe2cc5c534458578c004c1b3bb3f9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1546,
    "chunk_text": "Emily Ashby, Director for South and Central Asia took part. Immediately responding to the Executive Order of 02nd April, 2025 or once this announcement was made, the particular Report was submitted. So, that is with regard to the diplomatic relations.\n\nFurther, we held several roundtable discussions at the Lakshman Kadirgamar Institute well before this particular announcement was made, in which politicians and local experts took part. In addition, the Hon. President also wrote a letter directly to the United States President Donald Trump, highlighting the possible ways of mitigating these things, the actions that we could take and requested for collaboration to reduce these tariffs. That letter has already been presented to the White House and the White House has also acknowledged its receipt.\n\nTherefore, some views that have been spread over social media and the ideas expressed by some people that we have not taken appropriate action are not true; we have taken action. With regard to this particular situation, we have to understand that it is not a situation between only two countries, but a global situation. By the United States, a standard formula has been applied and there is no room for any country to proactively negotiate and get a concession. I will give you two examples. One is India. India went to the United States and had certain discussions about these tariffs, but still their reciprocal tariff rate is 26 per cent. That is, 50 per cent of the trade deficit divided by its total imports of US Dollars 85 billion."
  },
  {
